Requirements:
Inputs Demand, FaultA, FaultB BOOL.
Outputs PumpA PumpB LeadA BOOL.
Internal previous_demand := FALSE; episode_served := FALSE. LeadA init true.

At each scan:
if NOT Demand:
 PumpA false PumpB false;
 if previous_demand AND episode_served then LeadA := NOT LeadA;
 episode_served := FALSE;
else:
 select preferred lead if healthy else standby if healthy else none.
 if PumpA or PumpB then episode_served := TRUE.
previous_demand := Demand.

Ordering matters. "If either pump runs on this scan, mark served TRUE". Falling edge sees previous true and episode_served true then toggles and clears. Good.

Need output assignments every scan.

Could write:
IF NOT Demand THEN
 PumpA := FALSE;
 PumpB := FALSE;
 IF previous_demand AND episode_served THEN LeadA := NOT LeadA; END_IF
 episode_served := FALSE;
ELSE
 PumpA := FALSE;
 PumpB := FALSE;
 IF LeadA THEN
   IF NOT FaultA THEN PumpA := TRUE;
   ELSIF NOT FaultB THEN PumpB := TRUE; END_IF
 ELSE
   IF NOT FaultB THEN PumpB := TRUE;
   ELSIF NOT FaultA THEN PumpA := TRUE; END_IF
 END_IF
 IF PumpA OR PumpB THEN episode_served := TRUE; END_IF
END_IF
previous_demand := Demand;

Should satisfy all.

